{# Avatar for an author, from the author's Grav account upload. No upload, no
   image: the byline reads fine without one.
   size: rendered CSS pixels. The crop runs at 2x so the image holds up on
   retina, and Grav caches the result, which matters because account uploads
   arrive at whatever resolution the admin form accepted.

   User::getAvatarUrl() is deliberately not used: with no local image it
   returns a Gravatar address, which would send a hash of the author's email
   to a third party. #}
{% if author.avatarImage %}
{% set retina = size * 2 %}
<img class="post-avatar"
     src="{{ author.avatarImage.cropZoom(retina, retina).url }}"
     alt="{{ display_name }}"
     width="{{ size }}" height="{{ size }}" />
{% endif %}
